Once upon a time in the wilderness of tamilnadu, a boy named gokul stumbled unto a cave which was hiding behind a lofty waterfall.
he was curious but also cautious.
however, he was very determined in exploring the cave.
so one day, he packed up his bag which was almost as big as him and wentoff from his home.
he went deep into the forest.
the trees were green, the wind was restless and the air was pure.
it was very silent,
and it was very eerie.
but with his uninmaginable courage,
he walked forward, his steps unhalted he strayed further into the pillars of green.
soon he found the waterfall, but it barely looked so.
it was like the world itself was blue and falling.
he crossed the pressure of having himself broken,
and finally entered what seemed to be the entrance of the cave,
and there it was, a rabbit, so pure and so white,
he found it adorable and he went to pet it.
but he would soon realize his mistake.
the rabbit smiled, as it revealed a row of sharp white teeth was covered with blood,
fresh blood!
it opened its mouth and swallowed him whole.
and the cave was never to be found again,
as it remained as ancient as ever.
the end.

it is just one story in the long list of hundreds.

In another world, in another time, in a place full of blue, another boy with the name gokul found...
A parachute!
he was falling!
he grabbed unto the parachute,
and tried to pull it out.
he was falling at great speeds and the ground would soon reach him along with his death.
soon his hands could barely move,
he hands and and his body became numb.
he closed his eyes and embraced death as his body hit the ground.
the end
